    {
      "id": "comment-5e991eb8-9762-47fc-af09-303245f7d5a9",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Welcome",
      "position": [
        50,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "# Entangled Neurons - Quantum Correlations\n\nWhen qubits become entangled, measuring one instantly affects the other.\n\n## To Do and Notice\n\n1. **Create entanglement**: Apply a CNOT after a Hadamard\n2. **Bell states**: The four maximally entangled states\n3. **Correlation**: Measure both - they're always correlated!\n\n## The Spooky Part\n\nEinstein called this \"spooky action at a distance.\"\nBut it's real! And we use it for quantum computing.\n\n**Challenge**: Can you create all four Bell states?",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial introduction"
    }
